<usx version="3.1">
  <book code="NAM" style="id">EN_ULT en_English_ltr Tue Jan 07 2025 10:44:59 GMT-0600 (Central Standard Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Nahum
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Nahum
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Nahum
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Nam
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Nahum

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="NAM 1"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="NAM 1:1"/>The burden of Nineveh. The book of the vision of Nahum, the Elkoshite.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="NAM 1:2"/>Yahweh {is} a jealous and avenging God; Yahweh {is} an avenger and master of wrath;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh takes vengeance on his adversaries, and he maintains against his enemies.
<verse eid="NAM 1:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="NAM 1:3"/>Yahweh {is} long of nostrils and great in power; and to acquit he will not acquit.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh—in whirlwind and storm {is} his way, and cloud {is} the dust of his feet.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="NAM 1:4"/>He rebukes the sea and makes it dry, and all the rivers he dries up.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Bashan withers, also Carmel; and the flowers of Lebanon wither.
<verse eid="NAM 1:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="NAM 1:5"/>Mountains shake before him, and the hills melt;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the earth heaves before his face; and the world and all the dwellers in it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="NAM 1:6"/>To the face of his indignation, who can stand? And who can arise against the burning of his nose?
</para>
  <para style="q1">His wrath is poured out like fire, and the rocks are broken apart before him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="NAM 1:7"/>Yahweh {is} good, for a stronghold in a day of trouble, and knowing those taking refuge in him.
<verse eid="NAM 1:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="NAM 1:8"/>But he will make a complete end to its place with an overwhelming flood; darkness will pursue his enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="NAM 1:9"/>What are you plotting against Yahweh?
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will make a complete end {to it}; trouble will not rise up a second time.
<verse eid="NAM 1:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="NAM 1:10"/>For like tangled thorn-bushes and like their drink being drunk,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they are devoured—like dried stubble—fully.
<verse eid="NAM 1:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="NAM 1:11"/>From you came out a plotter of evil against Yahweh, an advisor of wickedness.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="NAM 1:12"/>Thus says Yahweh:
</para>
  <para style="q1">“{Even} if they are full and likewise numerous, also likewise they have been sheared,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he has passed away. Though I have afflicted you, I will afflict you no more.
<verse eid="NAM 1:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="NAM 1:13"/>And now I will break his yoke from upon you, and your shackles I will tear off.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="NAM 1:14"/>And Yahweh has commanded concerning you:
</para>
  <para style="q1">“One will not be sown from your name any more.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will cut off the carved figures and the cast metal figures from the house of your gods.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will prepare your graves, for you are worthless.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 1:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="NAM 1:15"/>Behold, on the mountains, the feet of a herald, announcing peace!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Celebrate your celebrations, O Judah, and keep your vows,
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the wicked will not repeat to invade you again; he is completely cut off.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="NAM 1:15"/><verse eid="NAM 1:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="NAM 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="NAM 2"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="NAM 2:1"/>A scatterer has come up against your face.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Guard the city walls, watch the road,
</para>
  <para style="q1">strengthen {your} loins, greatly fortify {your} power!
<verse eid="NAM 2:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="NAM 2:2"/>For Yahweh has restored the majesty of Jacob, indeed, the majesty of Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">although the plunderers plundered them and destroyed their vine branches.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 2:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="NAM 2:3"/>The shields of his mighty men are red; the men of valor are clothed in scarlet;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the chariot {flashes} with fire of metal on the day of preparing it, and the cypresses quiver.
<verse eid="NAM 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="NAM 2:4"/>The chariots race madly through the streets; they rush back and forth in the squares.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Their appearance {is} like torches; they run like lightning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 2:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="NAM 2:5"/>He calls his officers; they stumble in their advance;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they hurry to her city wall. The siege-shelter is prepared.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="NAM 2:6"/>The gates of the rivers have been opened, and the palace has melted away.
<verse eid="NAM 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="NAM 2:7"/>It is established: she is taken into exile; she is led away,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and her female servants moan like the sound of doves, beating on their hearts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 2:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="NAM 2:8"/>Though Nineveh {was} like a pool of water throughout her days, now they are fleeing away.
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Stop, stop!” But there is no turning back.
<verse eid="NAM 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="NAM 2:9"/>Plunder silver, plunder gold, for there is no end to the supply;
</para>
  <para style="q1">a wealth of all things of delight.
<verse eid="NAM 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="NAM 2:10"/>Empty and desolate and ruined! And the heart is melted, and a shaking of knees,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and anguish {is} in all loins, and all of their faces gather beauty.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 2:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="NAM 2:11"/>Where {now} {is} the lions’ den and that feeding place for the young lions,
</para>
  <para style="q1">where the lion walked, the lioness there, the cubs of the lion, and nothing made {them} afraid?
<verse eid="NAM 2:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="NAM 2:12"/>The lion, tearing enough for his cubs and strangling for his lionesses,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he filled his caves with prey, his dens with torn carcasses.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 2:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="NAM 2:13"/>“Behold me, against you—the declaration of Yahweh of armies—
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will burn her chariot in the smoke, and the sword will devour your young lions.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will cut off your prey from your land, and the voices of your messengers will be heard no more.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="NAM 2:13"/><verse eid="NAM 2:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="NAM 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="NAM 3"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="NAM 3:1"/>Woe to the city of bloodshed!
</para>
  <para style="q1">All of it {is} lies, full of plunder; the prey never departs.
<verse eid="NAM 3:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="NAM 3:2"/>The sound of a whip and the sound of a rattling wheel
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a galloping horse and a bounding chariot!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="NAM 3:3"/>A charging horseman and a flash of a sword and a gleam of a spear and many slain and heaps of corpses.
</para>
  <para style="q1">There is no end to the dead bodies; they stumble over their dead bodies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="NAM 3:4"/>From the many harlotries of the prostitute, pleasing in beauty, the mistress of witchcraft,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the seller of nations through her prostitution, and peoples through her witchcraft.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="NAM 3:5"/>“Behold me, against you—the declaration of Yahweh of armies—I will remove your skirt over your face
</para>
  <para style="q1">and show the nations your nakedness and the kingdoms your shame.
<verse eid="NAM 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="NAM 3:6"/>I will throw filth on you and regard you as vile; I will set you up as a spectacle.
<verse eid="NAM 3:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="NAM 3:7"/>It will come about that everyone looking at you will flee from you and say,
</para>
  <para style="q1">‘Nineveh is destroyed; who will sympathize with her?’
</para>
  <para style="q1">From where can I find a comforter for you?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="NAM 3:8"/>Are you better than Thebes, situated on the Nile River, water all around her,
</para>
  <para style="q1">whose defense {was} the sea, water her wall?
<verse eid="NAM 3:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="NAM 3:9"/>Cush and Egypt {were} her strength, and there was no end;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Put and Libya were among your allies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="NAM 3:10"/>Yet she as an exile went into captivity;
</para>
  <para style="q1">also her young children were dashed in pieces at the head of every street;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and for her honored ones they cast lots,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all her great ones were bound in chains.
<verse eid="NAM 3:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="NAM 3:11"/>You also will become drunk; you will be hidden;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you also will seek a refuge from your enemy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="NAM 3:12"/>All of your fortresses {are} fig trees with first fruits:
</para>
  <para style="q1">if they are shaken, they fall into the mouth of the eater.
<verse eid="NAM 3:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="NAM 3:13"/>Behold, your people {are} women in your midst;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the gates of your land opening have been opened to your enemies;
</para>
  <para style="q1">fire has devoured your bars.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="NAM 3:14"/>Draw siege water for yourself; strengthen your fortresses;
</para>
  <para style="q1">go into the clay and tread in the mortar;
</para>
  <para style="q1">pick up the brick mold.
<verse eid="NAM 3:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="NAM 3:15"/>Fire will devour you there, and the sword will cut you off. It will devour you as the creeping locust.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Multiply yourself as the creeping locust; multiply yourself as the swarming locust!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="NAM 3:16"/>You have multiplied your merchants more than the stars of the heavens; a locust stripped and flew away.
<verse eid="NAM 3:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="NAM 3:17"/>Your guards {are} like the locust, and your generals, like a swarm of locusts,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones settling on the walls on a cold day.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The sun shines and it flies away and its place is not known where they are.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="NAM 3:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="NAM 3:18"/>King of Assyria, your shepherds are asleep; your nobles are lying down.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Your people are scattered on the mountains, and there is no one gathering {them}.
<verse eid="NAM 3:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="NAM 3:19"/>There is no relief for your destruction. Your wound is severe.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Everyone hearing the news of you will clap {their} hands over you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">For upon whom has not come your endless evil?
<verse eid="NAM 3:19"/></para>
  <chapter eid="NAM 3"/>
</usx>
